    "updated_at": "2022-10-19T04:23:40Z",
    "body": "I agree this is an issue.\r\n\r\nAs discussed with @yuki3 in person, there are two solutions: we could make `Derived.prototype[Symbol.unscopables]` be `{foo: true, bar: true}`, or we could make `Derived.prototype[Symbol.unscopables]` be `{bar: true, __proto__: Base.prototype[Symbol.unscopables]}`.\r\n\r\nI suspect the former is easier to implement and a bit simpler. (And theoretically probably a bit faster for engines to optimize, but, if you're using `with` anyway, you're probably already on the super-slow path.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
